\cf2 \cb3 This glossary is designed to equip buyers, operators, and decision-makers with the core terminology required to confidently evaluate\'a0
\f1\b agentic AI platforms and partners
\f0\b0 , with an emphasis on enterprise readiness, customer experience automation, and production-grade deployment.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs80 \cf2 \cb3 Agentic AI Foundations & Core Concepts\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs40 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Agentic AI
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 AI systems designed to autonomously plan, decide, and act toward goals rather than simply respond to prompts. In enterprise environments, agentic AI enables end-to-end workflows by combining LLMs, tools (Actions), and enterprise Knowledge, as implemented in the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mavenagi.com/agent-maven?utm_source=web&utm_medium=blog&utm_campaign=glossary&utm_term=100-agentic-ai-terms"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 \strokec5 Maven platform}}.\'a0\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 AI Agent
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 A software-based entity that perceives inputs, reasons over context, and takes actions to achieve specific objectives. Unlike traditional bots, AI agents can adapt behavior dynamically.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Autonomy
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 The degree to which an AI agent can operate independently without human intervention. Higher autonomy increases efficiency but requires stronger governance and guardrails.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Goal-Oriented Behavior
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 An agent\'92s ability to work toward defined outcomes rather than isolated tasks. This allows agents to sequence actions intelligently across systems.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Multi-Agent System (MAS)
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 An architecture where multiple AI agents collaborate or coordinate to solve complex problems. MAS designs improve scalability and specialization.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Action Space
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 The complete set of actions an agent is authorized to take. Defining the action space is critical for safety and predictability.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Policy
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 A set of rules that governs how an agent makes decisions and selects actions. Policies ensure alignment with business and compliance requirements.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Planner
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 The component responsible for breaking down high-level goals into executable steps. Planning enables agents to handle complex, multi-stage workflows.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	9	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Executor
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 The component that carries out planned actions by invoking tools, APIs, or workflows. Executors translate reasoning into real-world impact.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	10	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Reasoning Engine
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 The logic layer that evaluates context, constraints, and options to determine next actions. Strong reasoning is foundational to reliable agent behavior.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs80 \cf2 \cb3 Memory, Knowledge & Context Management\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs40 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	11	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Memory
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Storage mechanisms that allow agents to retain and recall information over time. Memory enables continuity, personalization, and learning.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	12	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Short-Term Memory
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Context retained during a single interaction or session. This allows agents to understand conversational flow and immediate intent.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	13	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Long-Term Memory
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Persistent storage of facts, preferences, and historical interactions. Long-term memory supports personalization and institutional knowledge.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	14	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Vector Database
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 A specialized database optimized for similarity search over embeddings. Vector databases are commonly used to store agent memory and knowledge.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	15	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Embeddings
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Numerical representations of text or data that capture semantic meaning. Embeddings allow agents to retrieve relevant information efficiently.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	16	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 A technique that grounds AI outputs by retrieving relevant enterprise knowledge before generating responses. Maven uses retrieval patterns to ground answers in your Knowledge Bases, built from sources like Salesforce, Zendesk, Freshdesk, uploaded files, and crawled URLs.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	17	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Knowledge Base
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 A curated collection of enterprise content such as FAQs, policies, and documentation. Agents rely on knowledge bases for grounded responses.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	18	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Grounding
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 The practice of anchoring agent responses in verified data sources. Grounding reduces hallucinations and increases reliability.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	19	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Context Window
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 The amount of information an LLM can consider at once. Managing the context window is essential for performance and cost control.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	20	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Hallucination
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 When an AI model generates incorrect or fabricated information. Enterprise platforms must actively mitigate hallucinations.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs80 \cf2 \cb3 Models, Prompts & Tooling\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\fs40 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	21	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Large Language Model (LLM)
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 A model trained on massive text corpora to understand and generate language. LLMs serve as the reasoning core for many agents.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	22	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Foundation Model
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 A general-purpose model that can be adapted to many downstream tasks. Foundation models enable flexibility across use cases.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	23	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Prompt Engineering
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 The practice of designing prompts that guide agent behavior and outputs. Effective prompting improves consistency and reliability.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	24	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 System Prompt
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Instructions that define an agent\'92s role, tone, boundaries, and objectives. System prompts provide behavioral alignment.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	25	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Tool Calling
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Allowing agents to invoke external tools, APIs, or systems to complete tasks. Tool calling enables real-world action.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	26	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Function Calling
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 A structured approach for models to call predefined functions with validated inputs. This increases precision and safety.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	27	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 API Integration
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Connecting agents to enterprise systems such as ticketing, billing, or data platforms. Integration unlocks automation at scale.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	28	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 CRM Integration
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Using customer data to personalize and contextualize agent actions. CRM integration is critical for CX use cases.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	29	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Event-Driven Architecture
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 A design where agents respond to events or triggers rather than static requests. This supports proactive automation.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	30	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Workflow Automation
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 End-to-end execution of business processes without manual intervention. Agentic workflows go beyond simple rule-based automation.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs80 \cf2 \cb3 Orchestration, Reliability & Scale\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\fs40 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	31	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Orchestration
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Coordinating multiple agents, tools, and workflows into a cohesive system. Maven customers use orchestration to connect Actions, Knowledge, and workflows into end-to-end support processes (see\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mavenagi.com/customer-stories?utm_source=web&utm_medium=blog&utm_campaign=glossary&utm_term=100-agentic-ai-terms&utm_content=ent-grade-support"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 \strokec5 real-world MavenAGI case studies}}).\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	32	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Concurrency
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 The ability to run multiple agent processes simultaneously. Concurrency is required for high-volume environments.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	33	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Latency
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 The time it takes for an agent to respond or act. Low latency is critical for customer-facing use cases.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	34	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Throughput
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 The number of tasks an agent system can handle over time. Throughput reflects scalability.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	35	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Scalability
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Maintaining performance and reliability as demand increases. Enterprise agents must scale predictably.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	36	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Fallback Strategy
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Predefined alternative paths when agents fail or lack confidence. Fallbacks protect customer experience.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	37	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Escalation Path
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Routing issues to humans or specialized agents when needed. Effective escalation balances automation with trust.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	38	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Self-Healing
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Automatic detection and recovery from errors or failures. Self-healing improves resilience.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	39	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 State Management
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Tracking agent context and progress across interactions. State management ensures continuity.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	40	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Session Management
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Handling discrete user-agent interactions securely and efficiently.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs80 \cf2 \cb3 Governance, Security & Compliance\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs40 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	41	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Guardrails
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Constraints that prevent unsafe, non-compliant, or undesired actions. Guardrails are policies, constraints, and checks that keep agents\'92 behavior safe and compliant, especially when they call Actions or use enterprise Knowledge (see\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mavenagi.com/features/trust-compliance?utm_source=web&utm_medium=blog&utm_campaign=glossary&utm_term=100-agentic-ai-terms&utm_content=governance-guardrails"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 \strokec5 MavenAGI\'92s Trust & Security Compliance practices}}).\cb1 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	42	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Human-in-the-Loop (HITL)
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Human review embedded within agent workflows. HITL is often used during early deployment stages.\cb1 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	43	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Human-on-the-Loop
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Humans supervise agents and intervene only when thresholds are crossed. This enables scale with oversight.\cb1 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	44	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Governance
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Policies, controls, and processes that ensure responsible agent behavior. Governance is critical for enterprise adoption.\cb1 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	45	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Compliance
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Adherence to regulatory, legal, and organizational standards. Compliance requirements vary by industry.\cb1 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	46	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Data Privacy
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Protecting sensitive customer and enterprise data used by agents. Privacy-by-design is essential.\cb1 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	47	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Security
\f0\b0 \'a0\'96 Safeguards against unauthorized access, misuse, or data leakage. Security underpins trust.\cb1 \
\ls5\ilvl0
